  "runtimeScope": [
    "Relative quita/resta/reduce/baja instructions decrement exactly one proposed purchase. Zero remaining units withdraw that proposal. Over-removal and malformed counts require clarification.",
    "An implicit relative target that also exists in the current cart requires clarification. Explicit de las compras pendientes / de lo que vas a agregar scopes the operation to the proposal and preserves existing units.",
    "findProductsByExactAlias reuses the existing glossary and supports serving wrappers, articles and plurals while preserving qualifiers and conjunctions. All catalog owners are considered before accepting one result.",
    "Counted notes explicitly covering every unit of one SKU can update multiple existing variants together, preserving quantity, attributes, other notes and unrelated lines. Partial ambiguous distributions remain held.",
    "Scoped note appending validates the entire untruncated result before committing any line. Existing pending edit plans retain priority.",
    "Provider redelivery is deduplicated through the existing inbound message claim. Distinct new relative instructions each apply their requested decrement. JSON persistence, review, limits, intermediate questions, stale plans and mocked closure are covered."
  ],
  "developmentFindings": [
    "All eleven initial normal-entry contracts failed across relative decrements, unique aliases and notes covering all existing variants.",
    "The extended multi-line test found that joinKitchenNotes truncates to 200 characters before its caller checks length. This route now reuses editScopedCartNote so one oversized result preserves the complete original cart.",
    "A signed no-space count following an accented verb could be normalized into a positive decrement. The signed-count guard now removes accents while retaining punctuation and signs.",
    "General TypeScript caught optional quantities in persisted proposed purchases. The established one-unit default is preserved, while malformed fractional results remain held.",
    "The grouped-note route now respects a pendingReplacementClarification marker before applying notes, preventing an independent group edit from bypassing the held plan."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Provider responses, maps, persistence, Meta and order creation are simulated. Real-model wording and representative pilot results require additional measurement.",
    "Relative revision targets one proposed variant at a time. When that product also exists in the cart, the pending-purchase scope must be explicit. Unsupported or ambiguous revisions require a full-plan clarification.",
    "Aliases use the existing glossary, serving wrappers, articles and plural forms. New regional synonyms, unrestricted fuzzy matching and missing qualifiers are outside this route.",
    "Counted multi-line notes cover all units of one SKU. A subset spread across different variants and arbitrary multi-product transformations still need clarification or their existing dedicated paths.",
    "Distinct new message IDs represent distinct relative instructions. Provider retries with the same ID reuse the inbound-claim deduplication.",
    "Production promotion and generic Kamppo adaptation remain pending."
  ],
